  "body": "The Web Worker constructor has an overload that accepts additional information. Currently, you can do `{ type=\"module\", name=\"myName\" }`. This object bag isn't exposed inside the worker.  I believe there is work going on with some vendors to expose `name`.\r\n\r\nA common approach to constructor parameters is sending a message right after creation, but this pollutes the message handler as it has to look at every message to see if these one-time data are present.\r\n\r\nExposing the second constructor parameter inside the worker (as something like \"params\") would allow passing constructor parameters, and provide access to `name`.\r\n```\r\nnew Worker(\"path\", {type=\"module\", name=\"myModule\", instance=\"abc\"}\r\n\r\nconst instanceId = self.params.instance;\r\n```",
